#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287825 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f8a0b14-4d5c-5c97-adda-ad9333ee9989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439563} {:answer/id #uuid "dd74231f-397c-535b-b601-fd3c79196c9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439564}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439564} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc6cf2f7-d1dc-587c-98ad-df0c79eb39bd" :answer-field/key "$p=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440139} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b99de5ad-e5ec-584b-85db-f3fe0159078d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439565} {:answer/id #uuid "6a78a0f8-e11d-55e4-ae7a-bb450fd88339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439566}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439565} :answer-field/id #uuid "60fa672d-cabd-5202-b542-e29c05c6092c" :answer-field/key "$p=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440140} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0824bc4a-1fb6-5f8e-8f46-06f33e4a0f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439567} {:answer/id #uuid "4bccbe1d-f704-50a7-a7cc-0373aa409b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439568}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439567} :answer-field/id #uuid "b90240d0-5950-5b79-9a0c-e7150762e3ac" :answer-field/key "$p=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99e7c5d4-430e-5f20-88bd-00f87d74ace8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439569} {:answer/id #uuid "82587c1b-bbe1-5f58-a819-0bba3bb63520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439570}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439570} :answer-field/id #uuid "1827baf7-1958-50ff-a89b-0e47a7c1cf1e" :answer-field/key "$p=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1a6ffa24-d6e8-52ac-ac3d-5fab4f24df3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-18272" :question/problem "Given that $M=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & p & 0 \\\\ p-3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $det(M)=-23,$ find all the possible values of $p.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & p & 0 \\\\ p-3 & 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\begin{vmatrix}p & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix}-(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ p-3 & -1\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & p \\\\ p-3 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (3p-{p}^{2}) \\\\  & =-3-2{p}^{2}+6p \\\\  & =-2{p}^{2}+6p-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-23,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{p}^{2}+6p-3 & =-23 \\\\ 2{p}^{2}-6p-20 & =0 \\\\ {p}^{2}-3p-10 & =0 \\\\ p & =\\frac{-(-3)\\pm \\sqrt{(-3)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot (-10)}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pm 7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the solutions are $p=-2$ and $p=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e8ae76a-5493-54d3-aa37-0a50ee305014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285203} {:answer/id #uuid "673bedad-f93e-5e33-b575-f593287f0fa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285731} {:answer/id #uuid "6c8ba0a0-8fbb-518b-ab7a-8a3281a1a2e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285783} {:answer/id #uuid "d0973d57-7385-521c-beaa-e504e88a2f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286687} {:answer/id #uuid "d50df6cb-f315-5715-89b1-13015ccf48c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286726}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286687} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6846829-ca13-5ca4-aeb7-b66cd3e80412" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "109305f2-78e5-5de6-8ad6-74eb1cf5626d" :question/math-academy-id "q-20845" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z &=-1 \\\\ y+3z &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z &=-1 \\\\ y+3z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-z=-1\\,⇒\\,x=-1+z\n$$\n\nand from the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\ny+3z=1\\,⇒\\,y=1-3z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1+z \\\\ y &=1-3z \\\\ z &=z\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1+z \\\\ 1-3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d4f3f12-e7ea-5cce-ac19-8faedb3a2387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284898} {:answer/id #uuid "66ec6540-bc5d-5ef3-8c11-97293b066c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285727} {:answer/id #uuid "6834983e-fd55-5a02-900d-826e0996f634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285746} {:answer/id #uuid "6e59d671-de6c-545e-8595-763fe53fbc24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285803} {:answer/id #uuid "d1021de9-e761-5f3b-a765-8fd608dd3b6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286690}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284898} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1a2b9d1-c99c-51ec-b783-a734f5087196" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "37df46aa-880b-52ef-a085-52132aef293d" :question/math-academy-id "q-20967" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+2z &=-2 \\\\ 0x+y-3z &=3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2z &=-2 \\\\ y-3z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3z &=3\\,⇒\\,y=3+3z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand from the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2z &=-2\\,⇒\\,x=-2-2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2-2z \\\\ y &=3+3z \\\\ z &=z\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2-2z \\\\ 3+3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cd17603-f015-5fda-9003-c7df92c9f3fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285361} {:answer/id #uuid "5b09e969-3773-56db-974e-35c18e433e8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285619} {:answer/id #uuid "6f44e9e9-cd05-5cf4-883a-e05bc80beeba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285820} {:answer/id #uuid "eba0be1f-1d5e-5703-87ea-fb068e736905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286947} {:answer/id #uuid "f3fa88e1-060e-577a-9193-f6048fdbd1c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287023}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285820} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb3364af-4ff0-5722-ba18-646846604c56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "22a37001-42ac-5755-9c7b-a4e97d0ac7fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-20971" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 6 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 6 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+z &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=1 \\\\ z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nStarting with the second equation $z=1,$ we substitute into the first equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+2(1) &=1\\,⇒\\,x=-1-y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1-y \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-y \\\\ y \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "505018d9-5f40-5fe6-a2bd-8371d403497f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290974}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290974} :answer-field/id #uuid "31adadd0-5d60-5f06-b25f-16789378a818" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291902} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d591b4c2-08ff-5aaa-b44a-f770b77524f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291529} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fcd008a-d164-500a-b986-f81a0ace138f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291982} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50e80a16-e3c8-55c9-9435-066d6712c90c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290977}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290977} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b8794de-38d3-5c1e-a536-6f39850c2a60" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292226} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bff71819-0595-5166-8e24-1cbd5f3a41e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291459}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291459} :answer-field/id #uuid "db86b1f5-873e-5caf-abb7-1046d566f145" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d46bf19a-ed33-55bb-809b-da0d9d2e99d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-275511" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+2z &=5 \\\\ 2x+6y+5z &=22 \\\\ x-2y-3z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $1$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $6$ | $5$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | $1$ | $-2$ | {{field-4}} |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-1$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+2z &=5 \\\\ 2x+6y+5z &=22 \\\\ x-2y-3z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 22 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 22 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292865 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cd20551-e511-5385-ad3b-9f36caad9c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291027}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291027} :answer-field/id #uuid "14870852-5dba-5438-b80f-0294962b94c4" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291808} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99eb7f75-7610-5e51-a8a8-ea2f0aa74805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291299}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291299} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e8457af-c14e-5585-bda0-1873665d0316" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a08af78f-1333-5b89-bfe0-706c792d2caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291330}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291330} :answer-field/id #uuid "875d3970-b055-5c12-a79c-0f111817cb83" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292153} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36adad61-e1c4-5d23-8fcb-8c6eb215c8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290856}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290856} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1f3e50b-9242-52ef-956e-9a4abeae199b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f1f60738-9f75-548f-8757-47743135ac46" :question/math-academy-id "q-275545" :question/problem "If\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},$</div>\n</div>\n\nfind $AB.$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AB=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-4=2\\cdot -2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,6=2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,2=-1\\cdot -2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-3=-1\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle AB=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292866 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73870312-24b0-5710-9582-ace4d833975f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291128}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291128} :answer-field/id #uuid "61916db7-9570-5896-8478-8a654eab7267" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "375c7db7-262a-5420-9a53-a13dd2a5b997" :question/math-academy-id "q-275547" :question/problem "Let $L=MN.$ What is the value of ${l}_{22}$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$N=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}?$</div>\n</div>\n\n${l}_{22}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The full matrix product is\n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the $2$nd row in $M$ by the $2$nd column in $N$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{l}_{22} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =8+6 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ca215ee-0623-587b-9023-3636cc2853da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290882}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290882} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bc062b7-2d6b-5f91-84df-fab4dc97bf7f" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf79a280-af12-5e3c-8918-f31f6f1692f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291456}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291456} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d575b22-c24d-5b71-b048-2d6821f5eb59" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292072} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2777e86e-5def-5ed4-aa01-7b6a78c6f471" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290795}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290795} :answer-field/id #uuid "9328f2a1-09c3-56a0-9e6e-143199b95928" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292195} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "517711be-99fa-5cc4-928a-e39cfd30835f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290981}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290981} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b2c66e0-e219-51ff-ac06-6f99194b1abc" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95bfc9d0-38dd-5c62-9db7-d221f672eb17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291281}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291281} :answer-field/id #uuid "abe38b73-0e74-5167-9521-8f2884b60365" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292271} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0c345c6-6295-5859-bb04-8abe34723bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291640}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291640} :answer-field/id #uuid "e469f8ff-a383-5164-893f-961b9fa40f93" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9fed3a53-838e-5362-83b9-fbd6582bdbcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-275548" :question/problem "Find $AB,$ if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AB=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-5}}</td><td>{{field-6}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1 & (-2)\\cdot (-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c438cd2-2f9a-56e9-ba78-198237723b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290809}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290809} :answer-field/id #uuid "9902feec-4c1f-5bad-9074-0772c0883e74" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ff3bf305-a423-59b5-a761-0e3f9822d595" :question/math-academy-id "q-275585" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix},$ then $det(A)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}-5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & =-5\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-5(-21-(-10))-3(-3-0)+0 \\\\  & =-5\\cdot (-11)-3\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =55+9 \\\\  & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff81d498-e200-5357-94da-1cde068c1b4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291723}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291723} :answer-field/id #uuid "662aab82-835e-52a6-a86f-31ea8a24b31b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0de3688b-8fa3-5a15-976c-c08362b18d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290696}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290696} :answer-field/id #uuid "8079c99c-1a69-5aed-afe6-68e388cbfe16" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61e2285e-3ebe-5d82-b306-514b4f4eb771" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291048}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291048} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd3f99dc-5363-5fe9-a7f4-807e3dbcf354" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b02be14e-cb49-5b42-8e6d-3a07498cc78a" :question/math-academy-id "q-275781" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y+z &=-1 \\\\ x-y+3z &=2 \\\\ -2x+y-z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, and the inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe solution of the system of equations is \n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}, \n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}, \n$\\,z=$\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is \n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,y=0,\\,z=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14a3fe0d-b34c-5bb8-b1f3-dc5d8eca2468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290720}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290720} :answer-field/id #uuid "07e2a83e-a1a8-5c12-9edf-33f4a344c96c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6634bf9f-785d-5998-8bc6-6bf2bf22b822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291066}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291066} :answer-field/id #uuid "93a02cdf-28be-5434-93d5-c6e111efd86d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292197} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fec0e11e-aa0a-549e-b6fc-7edf5f309577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291721}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291721} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1d42cae-af03-514c-b698-ac6e1baf7763" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b1472133-fedd-5702-9754-ac7f5c7dd85b" :question/math-academy-id "q-275787" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+z &=4x+y+2 \\\\ x+y &=2z+2 \\\\ y &=x-y+z+1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $x=[x,y,z]^{T}$ of the system by computing the inverse of the coefficient matrix.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x-y+z &=2 \\\\ x+y-2z &=2 \\\\ -x+2y-z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3(-1+4)+(-1-2)+(2+1) \\\\  & =-9-3+3 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295135 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb31b60f-3050-5ef7-b4c3-2476ae1e52f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-146" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293849}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293849} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e0b8646-041e-54fe-904d-5fd7e7631312" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6794ccbb-8ffd-5507-a0b5-d0921c89d7f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-280387" :question/problem "If $H=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix},$ then $det(H)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & =0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-7\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-7(0-(-20))+2(-3-0) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot (20)+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-140-6 \\\\  & =-146\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295136 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18a27456-d8f3-561b-bb79-e130d6872c6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293031}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293031} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d897447-080d-5fa1-811f-5026bf48e4a4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ee0a6b76-25b3-5557-92d9-083561656751" :question/math-academy-id "q-280390" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix},$ then $det(A)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & =0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-2(0-0)-3(0-0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295137 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1339ed7b-7b32-5f2e-97a1-9339503ac331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293012}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293012} :answer-field/id #uuid "93fac66a-4741-5f19-907d-88bd6bf67c55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "602c9b3b-40e9-5371-929a-34e8b2aaccf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-280393" :question/problem "If $Q=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},$ then $det(Q)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =3\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+5\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 3)+2(4\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-1))+5(4\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =3(2)+2(8)+5(12+1) \\\\  & =6+16+5(13) \\\\  & =6+16+65 \\\\  & =87\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295138 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7756ac8b-4d3e-5612-bad7-e5a160c5a43f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293420}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293420} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7577202-1833-561f-80ac-32392b1ecb99" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5aadd6ce-d715-5a22-9944-d786941130cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-280394" :question/problem "If $R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},$ then $det(R)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(3\\cdot 2-5\\cdot (-1))+2(4\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 6)+0 \\\\  & =1(6+5)+2(8-30) \\\\  & =11+2(-22) \\\\  & =11-44 \\\\  & =-33\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "199cfd6b-b7c6-5ebd-9bb2-5a78fca81a8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "69" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293039}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293039} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca1eadfe-246c-5ca2-a02d-27c7056e56da" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294645}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4c583368-3601-5727-a2d2-942c7b9558d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-280400" :question/problem "If $W=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},$ then $det(W)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =5\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =5(4\\cdot 1-6\\cdot (-3))+2((-1)(1)-6\\cdot 2)+3((-1)(-3)-4\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =5(4+18)+2(-1-12)+3(3-8) \\\\  & =5(22)+2(-13)+3(-5) \\\\  & =110-26-15 \\\\  & =69\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295140 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b6fb57b-36e2-543a-ab01-e63593d507d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293544}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293544} :answer-field/id #uuid "9633885c-c66b-52e8-84a6-2cf06bb918b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b8c1908a-4170-5ad4-8920-81bd7dfc6050" :question/math-academy-id "q-280403" :question/problem "Given that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $det(A)=37$, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(F) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}x & 4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}3 & x \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(x\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 5)-(3\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =2(x-20)-(3+8) \\\\  & =2x-40-11 \\\\  & =2x-51\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $37,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-51 & =37 \\\\ 2x & =88 \\\\ x & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd58d80d-e3cd-55e9-ab3a-7f344ff3bcd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293792}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293792} :answer-field/id #uuid "de3f45f5-c264-5c0e-b8b4-960fb94c3f56" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294706}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b09153b7-90f9-5996-a92d-2d17cff9a754" :question/math-academy-id "q-280404" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}k+1 & 2k & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & k & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is singular.\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det & =\\begin{vmatrix}k+1 & 2k & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & k & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(k+1)\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ k & 1\\end{vmatrix}-2k\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -2 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(k+1)(5\\cdot 1-0\\cdot k)-2k(0\\cdot 1-0\\cdot -2)+3(0\\cdot k-5\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =(k+1)(5)-2k(0)+3(10) \\\\  & =5k+5+30 \\\\  & =5k+35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5k+35 & =0 \\\\ 5k & =-35 \\\\ k & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4fa7fe2-70f7-5b48-aad2-0f11a308a02b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293639}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293639} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff1893bf-705b-5320-b68c-49a5e5fad6f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cae37ba1-c114-55f8-b121-0094f150645e" :question/math-academy-id "q-280519" :question/problem "Given that $G=\\begin{bmatrix}x & 2x-1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & x+1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$ is singular, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det & =\\begin{vmatrix}x & 2x-1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & x+1 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =x\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ x+1 & -4\\end{vmatrix}-(2x-1)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{vmatrix}+6\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & x+1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =x(3\\cdot (-4)-0\\cdot (x+1))-(2x-1)(0)+6(0\\cdot (x+1)-3\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =x(-12)+0+6(3) \\\\  & =-12x+18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12x+18 & =0 \\\\ -12x & =-18 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7a14d7c-c976-5346-a0ff-1a7451eb909b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293594}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293594} :answer-field/id #uuid "744d1c09-7fab-597a-b711-9626275fab38" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294339} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e75f6dd-e85a-5f64-bcc4-624a0a4629af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292998}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292998} :answer-field/id #uuid "d728a0ab-06b9-5153-aa9d-039b19b0b1ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "854d343a-6ceb-5dbc-aed9-5a3bba384840" :question/math-academy-id "q-280540" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of $\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{2}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ x & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is $32$, find all the possible values of $x$ **in ascending order**.\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let’s use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}{x}^{2}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ x & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}x & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+0 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)(-2\\cdot 0-(-1)(4))-3(x\\cdot 0-(-1)(1)) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)(4)-3(1) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-8-3 \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $32$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-11 & =32 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =43 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{43}{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{43}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, **in ascending order**, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0455064-a7d8-59fd-ac77-33abf41ca336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293865}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293865} :answer-field/id #uuid "718e1993-6243-5b67-ad85-b48d5e4c1b0e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294333} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5474c54-161f-5c59-93d2-847eb2a1ab3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293891}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293891} :answer-field/id #uuid "904e7486-ae2f-53e2-a8b8-33a2fef9eb06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f11851f4-08f0-546e-8ec7-83f1d8f0d049" :question/math-academy-id "q-280541" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of $\\begin{bmatrix}x & 2x & 5 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ is $40$, find all the possible values of $x$ **in ascending order**.\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let’s use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}x & 2x & 5 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =x\\begin{vmatrix}x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-2x\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+5\\begin{vmatrix}3 & x \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =x(2x-4)-2x(3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 7)+5(3-7x) \\\\  & =x(2x-4)-2x(-22)+15-35x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-4x+44x+15-35x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+5x+15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $40$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+5x+15 & =40 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+5x-25 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-5\\pm \\sqrt{{5}^{2}-4(2)(-25)}}{2(2)} \\\\ x & =\\frac{-5+\\sqrt{225}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\pm 15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, **in ascending order**, the solutions are $x=-5$ and $x=\\frac{5}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299537 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85806f6e-3f8d-56f5-8841-0e3c0a47083a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298128}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298128} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f730fa1-b5c3-50b2-9976-270a3b0b824a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298906} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97ab1973-03cd-5f88-a18f-9217286fd9f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298209}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298209} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bda87eb-624b-5dc0-a615-09034a4dd617" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298994} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7150ff71-c085-5d5f-84bc-cd85d9ef931f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298040}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298040} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c396013-8c55-5d91-a811-c1d7554b13b5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91f9c034-96b3-537d-95ac-54136e6ff76c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298185}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298185} :answer-field/id #uuid "cda9e946-5a85-5e86-9781-1b1870f198bf" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "193f944c-d77c-5446-9a05-12850a3f60de" :question/math-academy-id "q-316961" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z &=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z &=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $-1$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $-2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $4$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z &=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z &=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299540 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answe