g matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $-5$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $4$ | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-4}} | $2$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $2$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x-2y+2z &=5 \\\\ 4x+3y-3z &=1 \\\\ -2x+y+2z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba42191e-a1b2-5cbe-be73-25f0fc307cc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298362}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298362} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e6ea13-72da-5a50-9831-59f3bb32ec83" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c62d600f-ef35-5c93-8a98-7c0b5d6bbb92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298418}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298418} :answer-field/id #uuid "525ad87c-5619-57d3-92a7-8525697b4703" :answer-fie